hat  the future journalists had about how  they would fit in this rapidly changing  media environment and i emphasized  excellence always stands out  to have an insatiable appetite for  learning  to pursue a variety of assignments and  to be inquisitive  evans i did a gymnastics event with  olympic gold medalist mary lou retton  and i asked her why the men  didn't do routines on the balance beam  like i saw the women doing  well she uh sheepishly  didn't answer the question  assuming i would figure it out pretty  quickly  and um  i did learn to ask better questions  after that  the third major lesson was to establish  the importance of having an excellent  foundation how are you doing so far sir  how are you american military hero  general norman schwarzkopf in a speech  to corporate titans stressed that in his  research of why many leaders failed  despite their impressive skill sets was  due to their lack of virtues  specifically character and integrity  roosevelt cheered as president of the  united states that brought to mind the  quote by former american president  theodore roosevelt  who said quote to educate in mind and  not in morals is to educate a menace to  society  the fourth and final lesson  it's not just about winning it's the way  you win  something i learned here at dematha  catholic high school from my coach  morgan wooten he finished an  incomparable 46-year career with the  winningest record in the country and  became the first high school coach to be  inducted into the naismith basketball  hall of fame  and just like pro football hall of fame  coach tony dungy  and the legendary college football hall  of fame coach eddie robinson the common  thread between these uncommon leaders is  that they never used profanity with  their players  they all ascribed to the belief that the  most effective four-letter word you can  use and model to ensure success in any  profession  is l l-o-v-e  [Music]  love  because love is not boastful or proud or  rude  it never gives up it never loses faith  because love  is more  durable and it will always last and now  i encourage you go out and knock them  alive god bless you  [Applause]  jb's parents drive and focus on  education and academic excellence proved  to be the foundation for his success he  was elected president of his high school  class and became the first  college-educated member of his family  graduating from harvard university well  just recently jb was honored with the  induction into the sports broadcasting  hall of fame  he is quite a role model he's amazing  he's an amazing person he's amazing  broadcaster i tells a great story i just  why i i stay glued to the screen when i  see him come on and he is as good a man  off camera as he is on camera he is the  best  colleague you could ever have one of my  favorite people

